{"name":"Mocha Syrup","hex":"#926f53","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mocha","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A coffee drink with chocolate syrup added, or a serving thereof.","A flavour that combines coffee and chocolate."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark brown colour, like that of mocha coffee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mocha"},{"term":"syrup","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any thick liquid that has a high sugar content and which is added to or poured over food as a flavoring.","Any viscous liquid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To convert or process into syrup.","To add syrup to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/syrup"}],"entries":[{"title":"Syrup","blocks":[{"text":"In cooking, syrup is a thick, viscous, liquid condiment consisting primarily of a solution of sugar in water. It typically contains a large amount of dissolved sugars but shows little tendency to deposit crystals. In its concentrated form, its consistency is similar to that of molasses. The viscosity arises from the multiple hydrogen bonds between the dissolved sugar, which has many hydroxyl (OH) groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Maltose_syrup.jpg/330px-Maltose_syrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrup","wikidata":"Q6584340"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Sirup_vom_Sirupier_de_Berne.jpg/500px-Sirup_vom_Sirupier_de_Berne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Sirup_vom_Sirupier_de_Berne.jpg/1280px-Sirup_vom_Sirupier_de_Berne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Sirup_vom_Sirupier_de_Berne.jpg/500px-Sirup_vom_Sirupier_de_Ber